## Step 5 — Dynamic filter bar

```
In my existing Dash app using dbc, create a filter_bar component
in components/filter_bar.py.

This is a horizontal bar that sits between the KPI row and the reason cards.
Users build their own filters — there are no predefined filter values.

It contains in a single flex row:
- dbc.Select(id="filter-column-select", placeholder="Choose a column…")
  Options: Driver, Source, Reason, Severity, Affected, Coverage
- dbc.Input(id="filter-value-input", placeholder="Filter value…", type="text")
- dbc.Button("+ Add filter", id="add-filter-btn", size="sm", outline=True)
- dbc.Button("Clear all",    id="clear-filters-btn", size="sm", outline=True, color="danger")
- A div(id="active-filters-display") showing active filters as removable pills
  Each pill: "Column = Value" + an × button
  Each × button has id={"type": "remove-filter", "index": i}

Store filters in dcc.Store(id="filters-store", data=[]).

Match the card style, button style, input style, and spacing already in my app.
Do not introduce new colors or sizes. Do not add callbacks yet. Layout only.
```

---

## Step 6 — Wire filters to driver table

```
In callbacks/investigation.py in my existing Dash app, add the filter callbacks.
The full dataset comes from the real data source already wired in my app —
do not define any default data here.

Callback 1 — Add a filter:
  Input:  add-filter-btn n_clicks
  State:  filter-column-select value, filter-value-input value, filters-store data
  Output: filters-store data, active-filters-display children,
          filter-value-input value (clear to "")
  Logic:
  - Append {"column": selected_column, "value": entered_value} to filters list
  - Rebuild pills display from updated list
  - Each pill uses id={"type": "remove-filter", "index": i}

Callback 2 — Remove a filter (pattern-matching):
  Input:  {"type": "remove-filter", "index": ALL} n_clicks
  State:  filters-store data
  Output: filters-store data, active-filters-display children
  Logic:  remove filter at clicked index, rebuild pills

Callback 3 — Clear all filters:
  Input:  clear-filters-btn n_clicks
  Output: filters-store data (reset to []), active-filters-display children (empty)

Callback 4 — Filter the driver table:
  Input:  filters-store data
  Output: driver-table data
  Logic:
  - Start from the full dataset already available in my app
  - For each active filter apply: str(row[column]).lower() contains str(value).lower()
  - Filters are cumulative AND logic
  - Return filtered list of dicts
```

