## Step 7 — Genie chat panel

```
In my existing Dash app using dbc, create a chat component in components/chat.py.

It returns a full-height dbc.Card matching the card style already in my app.
Structure:

1. dbc.CardHeader:
   - Left:  title "Investigate with Genie" — reuse existing heading style
   - Right: badge pill "SQL · Genie" — reuse the existing badge/pill style in my app

2. dbc.Alert(id="context-banner"):
   Default text: "Select a reason card above to focus the investigation"
   Use the info semantic color already in my app. dismissable=False.

3. Scrollable message area:
   div(id="chat-messages", style overflow-y auto, flex 1, padding matching my app)
   Seed with one AI message bubble:
   "I am connected to your Databricks policy warehouse.
    Click a reason card or ask me anything about unscored drivers."

   Bubble styles — reuse existing card/surface colors in my app:
   - User bubble: right-aligned, secondary background color
   - AI bubble:   left-aligned, success-light background, success-light border

4. Suggested prompts — 3 full-width outline dbc.Button (size sm), reuse button style:
   id="sug-1": "Fix rate if we backfill smoker_status ↗"
   id="sug-2": "Broker channels with most missing drivers ↗"
   id="sug-3": "Score uplift if all drivers fixed ↗"

5. dbc.InputGroup at bottom:
   dbc.Input(id="chat-input", placeholder="Dig deeper into any driver or cohort…")
   dbc.Button("Send", id="send-btn") — reuse primary button style

Do not add callbacks yet. Layout only.
```

---

## Step 8 — Genie API callback

```
In callbacks/genie.py in my existing Dash app, implement the Genie Space API callback.

Read credentials from environment variables already used in my app:
  DATABRICKS_HOST, DATABRICKS_TOKEN, GENIE_SPACE_ID

Helper function call_genie(user_message: str, context: str) -> str:
  1. POST {DATABRICKS_HOST}/api/2.0/genie/spaces/{GENIE_SPACE_ID}/start-conversation
     Headers: Authorization Bearer, Content-Type application/json
     Body: {"content": f"Context: {context}\n\nQuestion: {user_message}"}
     Extract conversation_id and message_id from response

  2. Poll up to 15 times with 2s sleep:
     GET …/conversations/{conversation_id}/messages/{message_id}
     When status == "COMPLETED" return attachments[0]["text"]["content"]

  3. On any error return: "I could not retrieve an answer. Please try again."

Dash callback:
  Input:  send-btn n_clicks, sug-1/2/3 n_clicks
  State:  chat-input value, chat-messages children,
          context-banner children, filters-store data, active-reason-store data
  Output: chat-messages children, chat-input value (clear to "")

  Logic:
  - Use dash.callback_context to identify the trigger
  - If suggestion triggered, use its label (strip ↗) as the message
  - If send-btn triggered, use chat-input value
  - Build context string from: active reason (active-reason-store)
    + active filters (filters-store)
  - Append user bubble, call call_genie(), append AI bubble
  - Return updated messages + clear input
```

---

## Step 9 — Assemble in app.py

```
In my existing app.py, assemble the full layout using all components just built.
Do not change any existing imports, app init, or server config — only add to the layout.

Import:
  from components.kpi_row import kpi_row
  from components.reason_cards import reason_cards
  from components.filter_bar import filter_bar
  from components.driver_table import driver_table
  from components.chat import chat_panel
  import callbacks.investigation
  import callbacks.genie

Replace the existing layout with dbc.Container(fluid=True):

  Row 1: navbar — full width
  Row 2: no-gutter dbc.Row full height:
    dbc.Col(width=9) stacked vertically with no added styling:
      kpi_row()
      filter_bar()
      reason_cards()
      driver_table()
    dbc.Col(width=3): chat_panel() full height

Add at the layout root (not inside any column):
  dcc.Store(id="active-reason-store", data=None)
  dcc.Store(id="filters-store", data=[])

Do not change the server run config. Databricks Apps handles the port.
```
